from pathlib import Path
import base64,json,mimetypes,shutil
import numpy as np
from scipy.io import wavfile
r=Path(__file__).parent;r.joinpath('delivered').mkdir(exist_ok=True)
A={p.name:'data:'+(mimetypes.guess_type(p.name)[0] or 'application/octet-stream')+';base64,'+base64.b64encode(p.read_bytes()).decode() for p in (r/'assets').iterdir()}
v=np.array(json.loads((r/'envelope.json').read_text()))
css='''*{box-sizing:border-box}body{background:#11171d;color:#f5f0e7;margin:0;font-family:Manrope}header{max-width:1260px;padding:24px;margin:20px auto}h1{font-size:30px;margin:12px 0;letter-spacing:-.8px}header p{max-width:900px;font-size:14px;color:#b8bec3;line-height:1.65}nav{display:flex;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:20px}button{font:800 13px Manrope;background:#f5f0e7;color:#111c27;padding:12px 18px;border:0;cursor:pointer}button[aria-pressed=true]{background:#f3d02c}.gallery{max-width:1260px;margin:auto;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:22px;padding:0 24px 30px}.item{min-width:0}canvas{display:block;width:100%;height:auto}.caption{font:500 13px/1.65 Manrope;color:#b8bec3;padding:12px 0}.caption strong{display:block;color:white;font-size:16px}.single .gallery{max-width:660px;grid-template-columns:1fr}.single .item{display:none}.single .item.active{display:block}footer{max-width:1212px;margin:0 auto 40px;padding:24px;color:#b8bec3;font-size:12px;line-height:1.7}footer a{color:inherit}@media(max-width:700px){.gallery{grid-template-columns:1fr;max-width:480px}}'''
fonts=''.join(f'@font-face{{font-family:{fam};src:url("{A[n]}");font-weight:100 900;font-display:block}}' for fam,n in [('Playfair','PlayfairDisplay.ttf'),('Manrope','Manrope.ttf')])
js='const ASSETS='+json.dumps(A)+';const envelope='+json.dumps(v.tolist())+';'+r.joinpath('scene.js').read_text()
items=''.join(f'<section class="item" data-state="{i}"><canvas id="frame{i}" width="1080" height="1920"></canvas><div class="caption"><strong>{title}</strong>{desc}</div></section>' for i,title,desc in [(0,'01 / Before capture','One speaker, two represented components. Gold occupies the surrounding air; coral stays registered to the speaker silhouette.'),(1,'02 / Selection in progress','A fragment of the gold field is being lifted into the recording strip. The source fragment and its captured copy are identical.'),(2,'03 / Captured record','The strip retains the gold category and an envelope of the existing narration. The coral source-associated component stays with the speaker.')])
notices=''.join('<h3>'+p.name+'</h3><pre style="white-space:pre-wrap">'+__import__('html').escape(p.read_text())+'</pre>' for p in (r/'font_notices').glob('*.txt'))
html='<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Curio / Capture study</title><style>'+fonts+css+'</style><header><p>CURIO BUREAU / ONE-PASSAGE VISUAL PROOF</p><h1>What gets into the recording?</h1><p>A single image construction, shown before, during and after selection. The portrait is an original generated illustration. Coloured material represents conceptual categories; it does not show anatomy or measured sound. This is a static study awaiting owner review.</p><nav>'+''.join(f'<button data-select="{i}" aria-pressed="false">{s}</button>' for i,s in [(-1,'All three'),(0,'Initial'),(1,'Intermediate'),(2,'Resolved')])+'<button id="headings">Hide heading</button><button id="safe">Caption guide</button></nav></header><main class="gallery">'+items+'</main><footer><details><summary>Scientific scope, assets and rights</summary><p>The source/captured gold fragment is a shared illustrative print texture. The coral layer is an abstract source-associated indicator, not a skull, an anatomical route or an equal contribution. A normal airborne microphone does not preserve the original internally transmitted self-voice component. Room/microphone response also matters. The recording trace is an RMS envelope of our existing approved narration, not an experimental comparison.</p><p>Original speaking portrait: generated with the built-in image-generation tool for this editorial illustration. Actual microphone: Anonimski, <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Microphone_and_cover.JPG">Microphone and cover</a>, <a href="https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/">CC0</a>; cropped/source-preserving matte, mirrored, composited. Owner textures/pinned fonts reused privately. No source artwork from the reference project is reused.</p><p><a href="https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9929504/">Orepic et al.</a> / <a href="https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-020-80095-6">Hosaka et al.</a> / <a href="https://www.nidcd.nih.gov/health/how-do-we-hear">NIDCD</a></p></details><details><summary>Font notices</summary>'+notices+'</details></footer><script>'+js+'</script></html>'
r.joinpath('delivered/Recorded_Voice_Capture_Study.html').write_text(html)
print('built',len(html))
